.TH CCO++ 1 "2026-11-20" "cco 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cco++ \- scaffold C++ projects that build with the cco build runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cco++
.B new
.I path
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cco++
.B init
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cco++
generates a project whose build description is the build tool: a
.B build.cpp
that includes the single header
.B cco.hpp
and drives compilation, linking, tests and
.B compile_commands.json
generation itself.
.PP
The scaffold writes
.BR build.cpp ,
.BR cco.hpp ,
.BR README.md ,
.BR compile_flags.txt ,
.B .gitignore
and either
.B src/main.cpp
or, with
.BR \-\-lib ,
a library layout with
.BR include/ ,
.B src/
and
.BR tests/ .
.PP
The generated
.B build
program has its own command line: run
.B ./build \-\-help
for its subcommands and options. The build API it exposes is documented in
.I cpp/API.md
in the cco source tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-bin
Generate an executable project. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-lib
Generate a library project, with a test target linked against it.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Target name. Defaults to the directory name.
.TP
.BI \-\-vcs " none|git"
Initialize a Git repository. Defaults to
.BR none .
.TP
.B \-\-ide
Write
.B .bsp/compiler-only.json
for Build Server Protocol clients.
.TP
.B \-\-build
Compile
.B build.cpp
and run it once after scaffolding.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print the planned files without writing them.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite scaffold files that already exist with different content. Files
under
.BR src/ ,
.B include/
and
.B tests/
are never overwritten.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress per-file output and the suggested next steps.
.TP
.BI \-\-cco-header " path"
Header to vendor. Use it when
.B cco.hpp
does not sit next to the
.B cco++
executable or under
.BR ../include/cco/ .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B build.cpp
Generated build description. It is the build tool; there is no Makefile.
.TP
.B cco.hpp
Runtime header written into the project root, copied from the installation
the scaffold found.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CXX
Compiler driver used by generated builds when
.B \-\-cxx
is not given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cco (1),
.BR c++ (1)
.PP
The API used by a generated
.B build.cpp
.RB ( cco::Workspace ,
.BR cco::Target ,
.BR cco::glob ,
.BR cco::run_program )
is documented in
.I cpp/API.md
in the cco source tree.
